    "description": "The ``async`` keyword is used in programming, and especially in languages like JavaScript, Python, and C#, to define a function that runs asynchronously. It means that it can perform operations without blocking the rest of the program.\n\nPHP does not support a notion of ``async``. The closest feature is called ``fiber`` or parallel processing, yet it is quite different from asynchronous. Generators also provide a pseudo-asynchronous processing.",
